                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Very entertaining short adventure hidden objects game. The story starts off with a dragon attacking a kingdom, burning every part of it with its fire breath. The King couldn't sit and watch his kingdom dissolve right in front of his eyes so he sent out a word to all the brave men \"The hero who kills the Dragon and bring its tooth will take the princess as his wife\" Of course this made all the men risk their lives in order to win the princess. And this where our young hero makes his appearance. You will be 'the fool' who is in for the glory and the princess. The story made me giggle multiple of times, the narrative voice did a good job telling the story. You'll help the fool to get the tooth in his own unique way.\n\nI liked the art style of the cutscenes, the hidden objects scenes don't look bad at all, I also liked that if you encounter a hidden object scene outside, the weather does change, it rains while you are trying to find the needed items. Also, some of the objects are interactive which is fun. The game doesn't have voice overs except for the narrative and the hero in the intro cutscene. But I didn't find it bad as I've enjoyed the town's people comments, you get many dialogues from all the encountered characters when you click on them.\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1350712473\n\nThe puzzles vary from easy to hard, I found them a little bit challenging but it gave the game some length as the story is pretty short. The game has five chapters, each one of them has its funny moments. Sadly there is no map, so you'll have to backtrack a couple of times but thankfully each chapter has only 5-7 areas to move back and forth in. It is worth it though, you wouldn't feel like it is a chore, it is a fun little adventure.\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1350864632\n\nSoundtracks of the game are really good and fit the theme and locations, but the art style of the areas are a little bit outdated, however, the game is an old one so I'm not going to complain.  \nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1350892454\n\nPros:\n+Nice cutscenes art style and some of the locations look good.\n+Good fitting soundtracks.\n+Amusing story will keep you entertained.\n+Well done narrative voice.\n\nCons:\n-No steam achievements.\n-No steam cards.\n-Some backtracking.\n\nThe game doesn't have cards or steam achievements but it is worth playing, and not having to worry about the achievements made the game very relaxing! I suggest getting it while it is on a discount since the game is short. definitely recommended.\n\n[quote]𝐹𝑜𝑟 𝑚𝑜𝑟𝑒 𝑟𝑒𝑣𝑖𝑒𝑤𝑠 𝑐𝘩𝑒𝑐𝑘 𝑚𝑦 𝑐𝑢𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑜𝑟 𝑝𝑎𝑔𝑒 [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/32399565/]𝐹𝑒𝑒𝑛𝑎'𝑠 𝐶𝘩𝑜𝑖𝑐𝑒[/url][/quote]",
